 {"id":"CF-085","title":"Satellite lanes inherit repo_url from their primary at mint time, so repointing the primary leaves the whole family on a phantom local: root — validate the root and fan the change out","status":"complete","priority":"P2","complexity":3,"created_at":"2026-11-03T16:23:35Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T16:56:01Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"13676ebbb517d73fecf822ebffce11668b12597762cf3e2bb563295596c32f24","evidence":[{"run_id":"e177011f","ts":"2026-11-03T16:54:23Z","tree_fp":"b9f715d5464a044e30583f3e3ce107511255cc73d19269ae1e720516da387799","artifacts":["scripts/lane_target.py","tests/test_lane_target.py","tests/selftest.sh","docs/SCHEDULER-ADMISSION.md"]},{"run_id":"dc095aa0","ts":"2026-11-03T16:56:01Z","tree_fp":"b9f715d5464a044e30583f3e3ce107511255cc73d19269ae1e720516da387799","artifacts":[".gitreins/history/2026-11-03/dc095aa0/verdict.json"]}]},"reasoning":"HYPOTHESIS (root cause not proven this tick): five code-factory-duckbrain satellites (-dogfood -pm -qa -releng -sync) carried repo_url local:/home/kara/code-factory-duckbrain, a path that does not exist (git -C => No such file or directory), while the primary code-factory-duckbrain and every other code-factory satellite carry local:/home/kara/code-factory. Satellite minting inherits the primary repo_url (scripts/add_family_lanes.py:73 and scripts/configure_family.py:163 hard-code the correct ROOT, so an older mint or an inherited-then-repointed primary is the likely mechanism); nothing fans a primary repoint out to its satellites, and no path validates that the registered root is a git root. Effect: every tick of those five lanes was identity-BLOCKED (lane history for -sync: 11 ticks, 1 committed / 8 dry_run / 2 failed). Repaired 2026-11-03 by partial PUT of repo_url plus the fleet.toml line (5 lines, diff scoped) — this row tracks the durable guard, not the repair. Fleet-wide measured class from the same scan: 307 of 790 local: repo_url rows resolve to a path that is not a git root (242 of them stand-in class), 12 rows point at paths that do not exist at all (python-audit-* family, mischief-chaos, ai-plays-poke).","acceptance_criteria":"A repo check rejects a project row whose local: repo_url does not resolve to a git root (git -C <path> rev-parse --show-toplevel must equal <path>) with a named error and a non-zero exit, a test in tests/ proves the phantom case fails while the real root passes, and the documented reconciliation repoints every satellite of a primary whose repo_url changed; verified by bash tests/selftest.sh exiting 0 with the new case listed and scripts/boardctl validate printing RESULT: OK.","capability_tags":["fleet","config","validation"],"worker_status":"complete","commit_hash":"d00577eadf50286572d3a2f317e439a1a043a49c","guard_result":"PASS","ci_result":"SKIP","worker_summary":"Repo-side guard for project-row repo_url: scripts/lane_target.py gains a repo-url check that requires a local root to equal the git top level (missing path / non-git dir / subdirectory -> named FAIL, exit 4; real root -> PASS naming root and HEAD). tests/test_lane_target.py adds 5 hermetic cases (30 tests OK); tests/selftest.sh section 19 prints the new PASS line; docs/SCHEDULER-ADMISSION.md documents the operator reconciliation that repoints every satellite when a primary repo_url changes. Pre-fix: 16 new assertions failed against the unmodified script. GitReins tier1 PASS + tier2 PASS, verdict e177011f, at commit d00577e on origin/main.","foreman_note":"Tick code-factory-2026-11-03-16-06-24. Selected CF-085 (P2, unblocked, repo-local) from the CANONICAL board at origin/main 247103c: the lane workdir proj-wt-code-factory-bankai-20261030 is a stale sibling checkout (61 ahead / 85 behind origin/main; its board misses CF-076..CF-088 and still lists CF-075, which canonical already closed), so selection and landing used the registered canonical root and the lane workdir was not written. One worker dispatched (gpt-6.1-sol/openai-codex) into isolated worktree proj-wt-cf085-20261103, branch cf/cf-085-repo-url-root; the foreman re-ran all three acceptance commands on the worker tree and again on merged main. Bindings a stranger can resolve: commit d00577e (git cat-file -t -> commit), tree d21549b0 (git cat-file -t -> tree), evidence fingerprint = sha256 of git show --format= d00577e, gitreins verdict e177011f under .gitreins/history/2026-11-03/e177011f/verdict.json. Hosted CI: the repository has 0 workflows and 0 runs, so CI is ABSENT, not green (ci_result=SKIP). Operator-side scope (repointing satellite project rows; 307 of 790 fleet local: repo_url rows measured as non-git-roots) is documented, not executed, and stays with CF-053.\n\nEvidence-binding reconciliation (same tick, after the close commit 9f20259). The gitreins CLI printed 'Verdict saved: e177011f' but no object with that id exists in either checkout; the resolvable verdict is .gitreins/history/2026-11-03/dc095aa0/verdict.json (task_id CF-085, passed true, tier1 PASS, tier2 PASS, cited here as run_id dc095aa0 and now committed to the repo). Binding defect observed, disclosed not hidden: because the judge ran from the control root with --scan-root, dc095aa0 records commit 0fbfe1f2 (the control root HEAD at grade time) and its commit.patch evidence item is 'git show 0fbfe1f2f219', i.e. a commit that cannot contain the graded change, while the same verdict's tier-2 rationale executes and quotes the worktree tree at d00577e. That is the class already tracked by open row CF-076 (a Tier-2 PASS bound to a commit that cannot contain the graded change); no second row is filed. Merit evidence stands independently of the binding: the foreman re-ran all three acceptance commands on the worker tree and again on merged origin/main d00577e. Memory leg: none:no-code-factory-scoped DuckBrain token on this host (25 role tokens present, none for code-factory), so no project memory write was claimed.","completed_at":"2026-11-03T16:54:23Z","branch":"cf/cf-085-repo-url-root"}
 {"id":"CF-086","title":"16 of 71 board rows embed absolute /home/kara paths, so a reader of this public repo cannot reproduce them — normalize to repo-relative or ~ and refuse new absolute host paths","status":"pending","priority":"P3","complexity":3,"created_at":"2026-11-03T16:25:42Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T16:25:42Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"cdbbf30ec4983b67ced60260135b79640cb0eb57623e6d3bac5427196f4acf75"},"reasoning":"Measured at 532e7b8 with git show HEAD:.coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl | grep -c /home/kara = 16 of 71 rows (CF-009 CF-011 CF-012 CF-013 CF-037 CF-045 CF-052 CF-053 CF-055 CF-073 CF-074 CF-076 CF-084 CF-085 PERF-013 PERF-014). This repo is PUBLIC (gh repo view visibility=PUBLIC). Two costs: the rows leak the operator username, and any path the row cites as evidence is unusable off-host — the same reproducibility defect CF-084 files for CF-011/CF-013. Filed by the sync lane 2026-11-03 rather than rewritten in place, because 14 of the 16 rows predate this tick and rewriting evidence text is a separate, reviewable pass.","acceptance_criteria":"A repo check rejects a new or updated board row whose JSON contains an absolute /home/ or /tmp path unless the row names why the path cannot be repo-relative; the 16 rows measured at 532e7b8 are normalized (repo paths repo-relative, out-of-repo paths to ~ with the reason stated); verified by running the check over the committed board with zero findings and bash tests/selftest.sh exiting 0 with the case listed.","capability_tags":["board","public-repo","hygiene"]}
